;;; ALGNUM, 2026-10-26).  Primes are galois's IS-PRIME-NAT (gal-char-vocab: p in NN and a prime element of ZZ-RING).
;;;   zz-is-euclidean-domain       Z is a Euclidean domain in the galois-theory sense (degree function |x|)
;;;   zz-unit-neg, zz-prime-abs-prime-nat, prime-nat-associated-equal, zz-prod-abs   the passage from primes of Z
;;;                                (up to sign) to prime naturals
;;;   prime-factorization-exists   PROP. 1.9, existence: a >= 1 is a product PROD-RING(ZZ-RING, p, [1, k]) of prime
;;;                                naturals p(1), ..., p(k)
;;;   prime-factorization-unique   PROP. 1.9, uniqueness: two such factorisations have k = m and a bijection
;;;                                sigma of the index sets with q(sigma i) = p(i)
;;;   prime-divides-product        PROP. 1.10: a prime dividing a_1 ... a_n divides some a_k
;;;   multiples-count, zz-prime-factor-exists, zz-coprime-iff-no-common-prime   first bricks for Prop. 1.19
;;; Route for 1.9: galois's euclidean-domain-is-ufd at ZZ-RING, then absolute values.
;;; LOAD WINDOW.  lo: catools-gal-vocab, catools-gal-b1, gal-ufd-vocab, gal-ufd (euclidean-domain-is-ufd),
;;; gal-char-vocab, gal-char (prime-nat-gt-one, prime-nat-euclid, zz-divides-small) -- all unwired, galois-theory;
;;; la-z2-diag (lzd-prod-succ), zz-number-theory (this bundle).  hi: none.  Library: algebra.
